---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Crumbs from "../components/Crumbs.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "../components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: SITE.url + "/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Services", item: SITE.url + "/services" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Managed advisory retainer", item: SITE.url + "/managed-advisory-retainer" },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Managed Power BI advisory retainer | Alluvium"
  description="After go-live the report goes stale, or it splits into copies. We keep one version current, without a large team on staff to watch it."
  canonicalPath="/managed-advisory-retainer"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article>
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <Crumbs crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { href: "/services", label: "Services" }, { label: "Managed advisory retainer" }]} />
        <p class="kicker">Managed advisory retainer</p>
        <h1>Keep one version of the report current</h1>
        <p class="lede">After go-live the report goes stale, or it splits into copies. We keep one version current, without a large team on staff to watch it.</p>
        <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>The project ends. The report does not stay still.</h2>
        <p>Someone changes a definition. Who can see which rows still matches last year. The refresh finishes when it finishes, not when the meeting needs the number.</p>
        <p>Then two people answer the same question from two copies. You do not need a bench of specialists to stop that. You need one version kept honest.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band band-alt">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>The same report, month after month</h2>
        <p>The copies sit off to the side. The report on the line is the one people still open.</p>
        <figure>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 680 320" role="img" aria-label="One report sits on a line of time. Two copies sit off the line, and their bars do not match.">
        <rect x="28" y="36" width="168" height="128" rx="5" fill="#f4f7fa" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="44" y1="56" x2="176" y2="56" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="44" y1="136" x2="180" y2="136" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="50" y="100" width="16" height="36" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <rect x="74" y="78" width="16" height="58" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <rect x="98" y="112" width="16" height="24" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <rect x="122" y="90" width="16" height="46" fill="#dcdcdc"/>

        <rect x="484" y="48" width="168" height="128" rx="5" fill="#f4f7fa" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="500" y1="68" x2="632" y2="68" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="500" y1="148" x2="636" y2="148" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="508" y="112" width="16" height="36" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <rect x="532" y="96" width="16" height="52" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <rect x="556" y="80" width="16" height="68" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <rect x="580" y="120" width="16" height="28" fill="#dcdcdc"/>

        <rect x="226" y="28" width="228" height="176" rx="6" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="3"/>
        <line x1="246" y1="56" x2="434" y2="56" stroke="#e7f1f8" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <line x1="248" y1="172" x2="432" y2="172" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="262" y="124" width="22" height="48" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <rect x="298" y="84" width="22" height="88" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <rect x="334" y="100" width="22" height="72" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
        <rect x="370" y="116" width="22" height="56" fill="#397fb0"/>

        <line x1="340" y1="204" x2="340" y2="252" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="48" y1="268" x2="632" y2="268" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <circle cx="60" cy="268" r="8" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="3"/>
        <circle cx="152" cy="268" r="8" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <circle cx="244" cy="268" r="8" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <circle cx="340" cy="268" r="11" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
        <circle cx="436" cy="268" r="8" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <circle cx="528" cy="268" r="8" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <circle cx="620" cy="268" r="8" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="3"/>
      </svg>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>What the retainer watches</h2>
        <p>This is care after the build. It is not a second implementation.</p>
        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card"><h3>The definitions</h3><p>The numbers the reports use, and how the tables connect.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Who may change a number</h3><p>And how that change is reviewed before the meeting.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Who can see which rows</h3><p>Updated when people change roles.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Refresh</h3><p>Timed to the close and the operating meeting.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>The list of reports</h3><p>Which one is next, which one should be retired, and whether people still open what you paid for.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band band-alt">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>Who it is for</h2>
        <p>A mid-sized company that already has Power BI and does not want a large internal team just to keep it honest.</p>
        <p>You still need someone inside the company who can approve a definition. The retainer keeps that definition from quietly changing after the project team leaves.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <RelatedLinks
      services={[
        { href: "/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights", label: "Dashboard optimization" },
        { href: "/data-project-management-change-leadership", label: "Analytics project management" },
        { href: "/power-bi-training", label: "Power BI training" },
      ]}
      posts={[
        { href: "/blog/who-can-change-a-measure", label: "Who can change a measure" },
        { href: "/blog/row-level-security-who-sees-the-number", label: "Row-level security: who sees the number" },
        { href: "/blog/gateway-refresh-7am-surprise", label: "Gateway refresh and the 7am surprise" },
      ]}
    />
    <CtaBand heading="See if a retainer fits better than another project." text="Book a session. We will look at whether the report is going stale or splitting into copies." />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
